<title>USA: Tobacco negotiators at White House for talks.</title>
<headline>Tobacco negotiators at White House for talks.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tobacco negotiators arrived at the White House on Monday for talks with Bruce Lindsey, a senior adviser to President Bill Clinton, but White House Spokesman Mike McCurry suggested that no deal was imminent.</p>
<p>&quot;We keep hearing that while they have made some progress, they have some issues between them that are not resolved and look very difficult in terms of their ability to be resolved,&quot; McCurry told reporters.</p>
<p>Asked if he expected a final deal to to be presented on Monday, McCurry replied: &quot;No. There'll be meetings, my guess, on balance, throughout the week.&quot;</p>
</text>
